TEXT 0 200 Left 2 !.op
TEXT 0 232 Left 2 ;BROKEN: no DC path to ground. Vmid and Vout reach the rest of the
TEXT 0 264 Left 2 ;circuit only through capacitors C1 and C2, which are open circuits
TEXT 0 296 Left 2 ;at DC, so their operating point is undefined.
TEXT 0 328 Left 2 ;Fix: add a bias resistor (e.g. 1Meg) from Vmid to ground.
TEXT 0 360 Left 2 ;Expected static finding: no_dc_path_to_ground.
TEXT 0 392 Left 2 ;NOTE: verified against LTspice 26.0.2 - this does NOT fail the run.
TEXT 0 424 Left 2 ;LTspice exits 0, solves the .op "by inspection" and only emits
TEXT 0 456 Left 2 ;"WARNING: Node vout is floating." That is exactly why the static
TEXT 0 488 Left 2 ;check earns its keep: the simulator accepts a circuit whose DC
TEXT 0 520 Left 2 ;operating point is not actually determined. In a larger nonlinear
TEXT 0 552 Left 2 ;design the same topology is a classic convergence failure - see
TEXT 0 584 Left 2 ;source_conflict.asc for a deck that really does fail to solve.
